le="border-bottom:1px solid black;" data-ref="81c0027d-59b8-4211-9b48-635f4971b2dc" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="e56d885a-9316-4680-8869-84ff28c83018"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="ae46f093-86ef-4b74-8381-a38f3e60f2fe"><p data-ref="a0812b22-a4da-4eb5-a471-a288bffa30ff" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a C program to construct a B-Tree of a given minimum degree. First, insert a list of keys into the B-Tree and print the inorder traversal after all insertions. Then, delete a given set of keys from the B-Tree and again print the inorder traversal. Finally, search for a specific key in the current B-Tree and print whether it is found or not.</p><p data-ref="95b4275e-930f-4827-b5e7-cb5eceeb6dfa" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="50d60b28-4130-4ffe-8d93-f239bba71794"></p><p data-ref="969596f0-67a2-4ecf-875c-703ffc38ea7f" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="09cbf31e-2ece-445d-a939-a263eb8e2115">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="49ae5f0c-ff55-4eaa-807c-715484652af8" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="24d74f4d-965d-490c-95c8-ee8a1fbb2e0a">The first line contains a single integer <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="c0e550ca-998b-41fc-853c-1a0ad46643e9" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="de83343c-b3fd-410e-8480-5d1ccec64468"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="4ac53840-5f57-4051-956e-b04492485534"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D461 TEX-I" data-ref="8de24be5-21c9-4d84-b260-5ec71f9a2e72"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="31e1a160-ddd5-43b9-9848-4e438829df25"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="225f6414-1a66-42c1-992d-07b8db57c4ed"><mi data-ref="78dae971-1dba-490a-8713-36437b224c70">t</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, the minimum degree of the B-Tree.</li><li data-ref="44166c0f-78f2-4582-816b-a55f57547b20">The second line contains an integer <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="ee559a89-de8c-444b-8e1d-c17e8833c1a6" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="60d85e8c-722b-448c-9466-a2ac3452c21d"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="d3b36b95-46f8-433f-bfb5-31401e6d693e"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="2d702c6d-8686-4b3e-a4d4-3caba29df3f7"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="a16ba822-736e-44a4-a179-f531deb9c443"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="f52ca763-275f-4ac4-815c-06b265474094"><mi data-ref="3db6212b-41d9-