ayed"><b style="border-bottom:1px solid black;" data-ref="fa17acff-45e3-4b0c-b455-be62ae3402c5" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="85d1eba1-1ad7-4a2a-b3a4-73dd6bf64dca"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="44a4792f-3e93-41e3-8bfe-9ad3bde27903"><p data-ref="e5b78fad-b5dd-467a-bc51-111ae84b192e" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">You are given <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="d617b133-54e2-455b-8189-24cb1e824bba" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="a0d30f8d-c3a1-4c82-b948-3243ce07ea1c"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="52785945-5c91-482c-ab2c-541f4cba3327"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="38001cda-6dcf-4c19-839a-9e733ff38230"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="36fc3848-f39d-4263-b9a3-edc24a710879"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="e2c19146-2b35-42f0-acb2-9bd65fccc9d4"><mi data-ref="12e3a795-27cd-497c-aacb-bdd16336092a">n</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> items, each with a specific weight and value. You have a knapsack with a maximum capacity <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="bda7d108-d47f-4fd2-840b-cc8f54c605e7" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="3e89647b-8ad9-4b19-89c5-7be3205cf314"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="47bbb4e4-7e2d-4069-99a5-6ec42aec3dc7"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D44A TEX-I" data-ref="c13424d9-64d9-4517-8b45-4bb4af0d3951"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="53548dd1-5d5b-4fa4-b480-f5f36f74b85d"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="c9fcba95-9575-44f3-84af-8ad7a609d531"><mi data-ref="c79d9b8e-f9f8-42eb-aee1-75592481be99">W</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>. Your goal is to select a subset of these items such that the total weight is less than or equal to <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="0bb6ab6b-7004-49e3-9810-71485fb1821e" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="53abc8cf-c0b0-4db6-a35d-0ef600168fc9"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="be781f42-26fd-4df0-b0ec-56269b73878a"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D44A TEX-I" data-ref="dbe4806b-6108-44fb-9bd6-dcda7249c9bc"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="62757db4-68f0-45e1-82bc-97cc1289c772"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="e3d38b0a-bdde-4779-ac5b-9cb09563c035"><mi data-ref="5ab7e054-ba3e-46e4-a42c-59c41fbaa205">W</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, and the total value is as large as possible.</p><p data-ref="64dd64ab-81f2-4967-a2f1-7ce654378fcb" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="65964341-74bf-4f8c-9f2e-cc2998fb7893"></p><p data-ref="a716ab76-bfc4-4af0-a4f8-369302e5d2c6" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">This is the classic 0/1 Knapsack problem, where each item can either be included once or excluded from the knapsack.</p><p data-ref="c65f487a-5148-4697-99c7-9f26a9363212" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="a1e91e84-c10b-4e62-b7f4-8ce95743430f"></p><p data-ref="c3e848bd-84c6-41b1-b47c-53bcb491569a" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="bcb5ee1f-1439-4547-8cc3-95be174414b6">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="8e798bff-f170-4a26-8fab-49f5c3ea5d3e" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="46af1537-fe28-4206-bd07-fd6da51c0545">The first line contains an integer <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="8e38ac5b-06d3-4660-8f24-adcb0043bc17" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="bfa46633-0ae4-4587-a67c-4d11d4a674da"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="976f470e-ca8b-44f9-80e0-88856dac5061"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="22386871-6604-46a3-ada8-d1c0b244e644"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="9c08aa28-09d9-4cc4-bafb-687ff6ce8903"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="537f4775-7e1f-41cb-b0b8-3d9e61698ca8"><mi data-ref="43148fc7-2417-45e2-acfe-e1b64ff7f2f1">n</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, representing the number of items to consider for the knapsack.</li><li data-ref="db582c9a-71a6-4236-9cc9-9bd56533d607">The second line contains <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="cb44174f-dc78-4e54-ac8d-13f6f66492aa" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="5465d62a-1668-4599-95a1-d716f6de2cb9"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="09535020-315d-43bd-8090-e67a072fb2be"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="c2366488-f4e8-4390-8fbc-f63109635ad9"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="3fe85776-9ed5-4f58-9c39-01d24e7cd9d3"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="e470c1f3-8707-4567-b507-d873bef1d460"><mi data-ref="20920ec0-1be7-4715-af94-52228f949a52">n</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> space-separated integers, representing the weights of the items.</li><li data-ref="91709eab-da98-4951-a0ea-08a7db5aae74">The third line contains <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="41894e4c-10d9-4449-94dd-ba42e892359f" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="cac29dc8-8efc-4f87-9283-5ee4a9b0c043"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="845014e7-6ee8-4552-8f33-d2f5c54ae790"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D45B TEX-I" data-ref="c69456f8-9773-4ab8-ade4-6b78d384b27a"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="f89debd6-04b5-4a33-8919-e2ed5f3d3b3a"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="c1abf07a-4ca2-4395-b19b-2725f1fd3422"><mi data-ref="814db3f0-4932-448c-8983-0f618d313546">n</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> space-separated integers, representing the values of the items, corresponding to their weights.</li><li data-ref="0cca4d18-21cf-4857-af09-580127f1529b">The fourth line contains an integer <mjx-container class="MathJax" jax="CHTML" style="font-size: 119.5%; position: relative;" data-ref="fa982d3d-3d07-4572-a4eb-5eb3b575e729" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><mjx-math class="MJX-TEX" aria-hidden="true" data-ref="50796ddf-b0d3-42ab-b4e8-343eef4bbe23"><mjx-mi class="mjx-i" data-ref="bb73dc09-a606-4f55-b729-a566e0f1135f"><mjx-c class="mjx-c1D44A TEX-I" data-ref="97e70d2a-1d08-4e09-98bf-44e620596a78"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable="on" display="inline" data-ref="c694d762-8cdf-4663-88cd-66decf78f665"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" data-ref="9989deea-cdde-4ab0-abd3-2b763dbda7da"><mi data-ref="38edcd9a-2ae3-484b-af5b-b57bc0191e9f">W</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>, representing the capacity of the knapsack.</li></ul><p data-ref="cbbbf3a5-a962-4ca1-a86c-60cc6c26857c" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="460f6018-9418-43c1-a682-7264204b5406"></p><p data-ref="60f0c4cf-24f3-4f83-b5cb-910de48fae56" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="61bd9c7e-5524-4127-92f6-6a1062c45c87">Ou