lid black;" data-ref="20728612-aae0-4297-a698-d2239361b58d" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="7b3b68c2-76e7-4584-9f83-ce0b6b9fad57"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="ec8c1b86-0510-424f-873c-6da15c0dafb1"><p data-ref="2900329f-4791-4db8-acb8-daecc4430c73" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a C program to solve the 0/1 Knapsack Problem using backtracking approach. The program aims to maximize the total value of items that can be included in a knapsack without exceeding its capacity</p><p data-ref="e9eb6a9c-071e-470d-87c3-8d0effd2d44b" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="1fd0faad-4bc8-4277-b023-bae27a35d369"></p><p data-ref="e6ac3650-367b-48a3-b4e1-bf410d058e46" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="5190534f-da2e-4ef5-ad35-1af797b40501">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="575ae69a-c7f1-4e05-9640-2e9b0f14ddb8" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-count